---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site, b } from "../site.config";

const privacyPolicySchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "@id": `${site.url}/privacy-policy#webpage`,
  url: `${site.url}/privacy-policy`,
  name: `Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`,
  description: `Full ${site.name} privacy policy: what stays on your device, GDPR/CCPA rights, cookies, analytics, advertising, and how to contact us.`,
  inLanguage: site.locale,
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${site.url}/#website` },
  publisher: { "@id": `${site.url}/#organization` },
};

const lastUpdated = "2026-07-30";
const effectiveDate = "2026-07-30";
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`Full ${site.name} privacy policy: GDPR & CCPA compliant. Your picked colors never leave your device; we disclose the analytics and advertising cookies we use.`}
  jsonLd={[privacyPolicySchema]}
>
  <section class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="heading-section text-[36px] sm:text-[44px] mb-3 text-balance">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-[13px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)] mb-8">
        Last updated: {lastUpdated} · Effective: {effectiveDate}
      </p>

      <p class="text-[18px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-10">
        <strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">TL;DR:</strong> {site.name} runs 100% in your browser.
        The colors you pick are handled entirely on your device and are never
        collected, stored, or transmitted to us. We do use privacy-respecting
        analytics and may show ads to keep the tool free — both are fully
        disclosed below. For the architectural deep-dive on the on-device
        design, see <a href={b("/privacy")} class="prose-link">Privacy by design</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">1. Who we are (data controller)</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        This site is operated by <span class="text-[var(--color-fg)] font-medium">{site.author}</span>
        ({site.jurisdiction}), the data controller for the limited processing
        described here. For any privacy question, contact
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="prose-link">{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">2. Your colors never leave your device</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-3">
        The core of the tool is deliberately zero-knowledge:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>The colors you pick are returned directly by your browser (via the <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">EyeDropper</code> API) to JavaScript running on this page. They are never sent over the network.</li>
        <li>Screenshot frames from the screenshot picker are held only in browser memory while the modal is open, then freed. They are never uploaded.</li>
        <li>There are <strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">no accounts</strong> — no sign-up, no login, no profile.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">3. What stays on your device</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-3">Some data is stored locally in your browser and never leaves your device:</p>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Color palette history</strong> — stored in <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">localStorage</code> under the key <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">screencolorpicker:palette:v1</code>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Theme preference</strong> (dark/light) — stored in <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">localStorage</code> under <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">screencolorpicker:theme</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        You can wipe this data anytime via your browser's "Clear site data"
        setting, or use the "Clear all" button in the recent palette panel.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">4. Information we do process</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-3">
        To operate and improve a free tool, a small amount of standard,
        non-identifying data is processed:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Analytics (Google Analytics 4).</strong> We use GA4 to understand aggregate, anonymized usage — page views, approximate region, device/browser type. GA4 sets cookies (see §5). We do not use it to identify you personally and IP anonymization is applied.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">CDN / server logs.</strong> Our host (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Cloudflare Pages</a>) logs basic request metadata (IP address, user agent, request URL) for abuse prevention and infrastructure operations, typically retained ~30 days.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">5. Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-3">
        The tool itself sets no cookies — its state lives in <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">localStorage</code>.
        Cookies are set by the third-party services we use:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Analytics cookies</strong> — Google Analytics 4 sets cookies (e.g. <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">_ga</code>) to distinguish anonymous visitors and measure aggregate usage.</li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Advertising cookies (if shown).</strong> We may display ads served by Google AdSense.
          Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies (such as the <strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">DART</strong> cookie) to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
          Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this and/or other sites on the Internet.
          You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Google Ads Settings</a>,
          or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
          <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">6. Third-party services</h2>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Cloudflare Pages</strong> — hosts the static HTML/CSS/JS. <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Google Analytics 4</strong> — privacy-respecting, aggregate usage analytics. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Google AdSense</strong> (if ads are shown) — contextual advertising. <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">How Google uses advertising data</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Google Fonts</strong> — serves the Geist font family from <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-[var(--color-fg)]">fonts.googleapis.com</code>. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Privacy policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">7. Your rights (GDPR / CCPA)</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-3">
        If you are in the EEA/UK (GDPR) or California (CCPA), you have rights
        over your personal data. Because we process only anonymized, aggregate
        data and never build a profile of you, most requests are trivially
        satisfied. To exercise any right, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="prose-link">{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Access / portability:</strong> we hold no identifiable data tied to you; your palette lives in your browser's localStorage and can be exported via dev tools.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Deletion:</strong> clear your browser site data to remove local state; you can opt out of analytics/ads cookies via the links in §5.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Object / restrict processing:</strong> use browser controls or the opt-out links in §5 to stop analytics and advertising cookies.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Opt out of sale/sharing (CCPA):</strong> we do not sell your personal information. You can limit ad personalization via <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="prose-link">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Lawful basis (GDPR):</strong> legitimate interest for aggregate analytics and, where required, consent for personalized advertising.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">8. International data transfers</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        Our providers (Cloudflare, Google) operate globally and may process
        data in countries outside your own, including the United States, under
        appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">9. Data retention</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        Local data (palette, theme) persists in your browser until you clear it.
        CDN logs are retained by Cloudflare for ~30 days. Analytics data is
        retained per Google's configured retention window. We keep no separate
        database of our own.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">10. Children</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        {site.name} is suitable for all ages and does not knowingly collect
        personal information from anyone, including children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7] mb-6">
        We may update this policy as the product evolves. Material changes
        will be reflected in the "Last updated" date at the top. Continued
        use after changes constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-card text-[22px] mt-12 mb-4">12. Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-[1.7]">
        For any privacy question, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="prose-link">{site.contactEmail}</a>
        or visit the <a href={b("/contact")} class="prose-link">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
